##Data Visualization
In order to plot the image we will use the RGB scheeme:

#layer1 = red wavelength, layer 2= green wavelength layer 3 = blue wavelength
im.plotRGB(group, r=1, g=2, b=3)

The image is flipped, so I can solve the problem by the flip()function:

group<-flip(group)
im.plotRGB(group, r=1, g=2, b=3)

The output plot can be exorted by the png() function
```r
png("group_photo.png")
im.plotRGB(group, r=1, g=2, b=3)
dev.off()
```
